# DEPLOY STEP, NOT OPTIONAL: `connect-src 'self'` and `img-src` below are the
# local-only values. vite.config.ts derives both from VITE_API_BASE_URL and
# VITE_STORAGE_ORIGIN, so dev and `vite preview` silently work while this static
# file does not. Ship it unchanged to a host where the API and Supabase are on
# other origins and every API call and every signed shop photo is CSP-blocked in
# production, with nothing failing beforehand to warn you. Add the exact HTTPS
# (and WSS, if used) origins here before the first deploy. See
# docs/security/SECURITY.md.
#
# script-src carried 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for Rive until 2026-08-01. Rive is
# deleted and nothing else compiles WebAssembly, so it is gone. Keep script-src
# at bare 'self' and never add 'unsafe-eval' to quiet a DevTools notice.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self'; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://tile.openstreetmap.org https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
